dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.030269999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":20.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.5,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":50.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Enphase Energy, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, designs, develops, manufactures, and sells home energy solutions for the solar photovoltaic industry in the United States and internationally. The company offers semiconductor-based microinverter that converts energy at the individual solar module level and combines with its proprietary networking and software technologies to provide energy monitoring and control. It also provides microinverter units and related accessories; IQ Battery and related accessories; IQ PowerPack 1500 and related accessories; IQ Combiner, IQ Gateway, and IQ Energy Router; cloud-based monitoring service; and electric vehicle charging solutions, as well as design, proposal, permitting, installation and solar appointment generation services, and Enphase Care services. The company sells its solutions to solar distributors; and directly to large installers, original equipment manufacturers, strategic partners, and homeowners, as well as through its legacy product upgrade program or online store. Enphase Energy, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Fremont, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Badrinarayanan  Kothandaraman | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $757,334 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $513K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 16%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $75K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Enphase Energy, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $3.8B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -14% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +2.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 70% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 61-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 35%.","The business throws off $96M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.79\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 35\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 15% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 423% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.225160817392791},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (26.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $5.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-5507910.25},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Technology peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Is Next For Enphase Energy (NASDAQ:ENPH) After Its Latest Update?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/energy/what-is-next-for-enphase-energy-nasdaqenph-after-its-latest-update","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793910720.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3 US Manufacturing Stocks Riding The Battery Materials Onshoring Shift","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nasdaq-enph/enphase-energy/news/3-us-manufacturing-stocks-riding-the-battery-materials-onsho","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793989463.822,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.153,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Oil Rebounds Toward $100 as Democrats\u2019 Sweep Rattles Energy Stocks","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/oil-rebounds-toward-100-democrats-010000633